---
const lanes = [
  {
    capability: 'Components',
    work: 'Custom Elements + Shadow DOM',
    status: 'HTML platform',
    platform: 'Reusable element identity, lifecycle, encapsulation, slots',
    remains: 'Application state, data flow, routing, composition policy',
  },
  {
    capability: 'Reactivity',
    work: 'TC39 Signals',
    status: 'Stage 1 proposal',
    platform: 'A possible common signal graph and auto-tracking substrate',
    remains: 'Effects, scheduling, ownership, rendering coordination',
  },
  {
    capability: 'Navigation',
    work: 'Navigation API',
    status: 'HTML Living Standard',
    platform: 'Application-oriented navigation and history primitives',
    remains: 'Route trees, loaders, layouts, authorization, conventions',
  },
  {
    capability: 'Transitions',
    work: 'View Transitions',
    status: 'CSSWG editor draft',
    platform: 'Browser-coordinated visual transition machinery',
    remains: 'Product meaning, timing policy, state coordination',
  },
  {
    capability: 'Dynamic DOM',
    work: 'DOM Parts',
    status: 'Web Components proposal',
    platform: 'Addressable mutable positions and content in DOM',
    remains: 'Template language, compiler strategy, rendering policy',
  },
  {
    capability: 'Controls',
    work: 'Open UI',
    status: 'W3C Community Group',
    platform: 'Common control anatomy, behavior, styling and accessibility work',
    remains: 'Product-specific composition and application behavior',
  },
];
---

<figure class="standards-landscape not-prose">
  <header>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Standards landscape · Sep 17, 2026</p>
      <h3>Not one roadmap. A set of pressure points.</h3>
    </div>
    <p class="dek">
      Different groups are standardizing different layers. The repeated pattern is selective platform absorption, not a coordinated replacement of frameworks.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="table" role="table" aria-label="Frontend standards landscape">
    <div class="table-head" role="row">
      <span role="columnheader">Capability</span>
      <span role="columnheader">Platform work</span>
      <span role="columnheader">What moves downward</span>
      <span role="columnheader">What still stays above</span>
    </div>

    {lanes.map((lane, index) => (
      <div class="row" role="row">
        <div class="capability" role="cell">
          <span class="index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <strong>{lane.capability}</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="work" role="cell">
          <strong>{lane.work}</strong>
          <span class="status">{lane.status}</span>
        </div>
        <p role="cell">{lane.platform}</p>
        <p role="cell">{lane.remains}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    The lower layer grows selectively. Frameworks remain responsible for higher-level coordination and policy even when a primitive becomes native.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .standards-landscape {
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .standards-landscape :global(p),
  .standards-landscape :global(h3) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  header {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 1.35rem;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .index,
  .status,
  .table-head {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-ui);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: 0.45rem !important;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.8rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .dek {
    max-width: 35rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .table-head {
    display: none;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.48rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .row {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .row:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .capability,
  .work {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .capability strong,
  .work strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .index {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.48rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .status {
    margin-left: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.22rem 0.45rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.43rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .row > p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  figcaption {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (min-width: 780px) {
    header {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.9fr);
      align-items: end;
      padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
    }

    .table-head,
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 0.75fr 1fr 1.25fr 1.25fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .table-head {
      display: grid;
      padding: 0.7rem 1.2rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      background: var(--bg-secondary);
    }

    .row {
      align-items: start;
      padding: 0.95rem 1.2rem;
    }

    .capability,
    .work {
      display: block;
    }

    .capability strong,
    .work strong {
      display: block;
    }

    .index {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }

    .status {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 0.45rem;
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
